13
00:55:42,857 --> 00:55:48,857
The Night Strangler is an American made-for-television horror film that first
aired on ABC on January 16, 1973, as a sequel to The Night Stalker.

14
01:00:00,000 --> 01:00:06,000
In the film, Carl Kolchak (played by Darren McGavin), an investigative reporter assigned to series
of killings, comes to suspect the murderer is an immortal with superhuman strength.

15
01:04:17,142 --> 01:04:23,142
The Night Strangler, though not as popular as its predecessor, garnered both strong ratings and
positive reviews, eventually prompting ABC to order a TV series Kolchak: The Night Stalker.

16
01:08:34,285 --> 01:08:40,285
Neither writer Richard Matheson nor producer/director
Dan Curtis was involved in the TV series.

17
01:12:51,428 --> 01:12:57,428
In the United States, the TV movie ran (without
commercials) approximately 74 minutes.

18
01:17:08,571 --> 01:17:14,571
ABC planned to release the film overseas as a theatrical release and had
additional footage shot, rounding out the movie to 90 minutes.

19
01:21:25,714 --> 01:21:31,714
The film explores themes of sequel, investigative journalist, occult detective.

20
01:25:42,857 --> 01:25:48,857
The tone is dark and mind_bending.
